/* ============ end of features: Sign in with Apple and Google ============ */
/* ============ features: sign-in feedback (working buttons, "Check your email", the confirm link landing) ============ */
/* Andrew, 2026-11-08: confirming an email must be obvious. Every sign-in button shows it is working (and says so if it takes a while);
   after "Create account" or "Email me a reset link" the form gives way to a "Check your email" card with the exact address, Resend with
   a countdown, Change email and a shortcut to the mail app. After sign-up that card also waits for the confirmation and continues by itself
   (it tries the same email and password again every few seconds and whenever the page comes back into view), so someone who confirms on
   their phone's mail and comes back to the iPhone or Android app, or to another tab, lands in their workspace without doing anything. The
   confirm link itself lands on "Email confirmed, signing you in"; a used or expired link lands on a card that sends a new one.
   Emails carry links, not codes (the server's templates), so there is no code field. English or Spanish, like the rest of the sign-in. */
